==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*kattuz}}. Cognate with {{etyl|osx|-}} {{m|osx|katto}}, {{etyl|non|-}} {{m|non|kǫttr}} ({{etyl|sv|-}} {{m|sv|katt}}), {{etyl|goh|-}} {{m|goh|kazzo}}. The word existed in the Germanic languages in a female gender also, represented in Old English by {{m|ang|catte}}. The word appears to be related to {{etyl|LL.|-}} {{m|la|cattus}} as well as to similar words in the Slavic and Celtic languages, but the ultimate source is uncertain.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈkatː/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|m}}

# [[cat]]

